<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0">

<hick:when test="rust-frontend-lib">

## Rust Frontend Library

This library contains shared business logic written in Rust that compiles to multiple targets:
- **WebAssembly** — For React SPA and browser extensions via wasm-bindgen
- **Native FFI** — For SwiftUI, Android, and Avalonia via UniFFI

This architecture allows you to write performance-critical or security-sensitive code once
in Rust and share it across all platforms with type-safe bindings.

### Project Configuration

The Cargo.toml configures both WASM and FFI targets. The `crate-type` includes both
`cdylib` (for WASM/FFI) and `lib` (for Rust consumers like the backend):

<hick:file path="rust-lib/Cargo.toml">[package]
name = "<hick:val name="project_name" />-core"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "<hick:val name="rust_edition" />"

[lib]
crate-type = ["cdylib", "lib"]
name = "<hick:val name="project_name" />_core"

[dependencies]
# Serialization
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1"

# Error handling
thiserror = "2"
<hick:when test="sqlite">
# SQLite (common dependencies)
chrono = { version = "0.4", features = ["serde"] }
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">
# Iroh P2P networking (common dependencies)
iroh-base = "0.31"
</hick:when>

# WASM support (only included for wasm32 target)
[target.'cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")'.dependencies]
wasm-bindgen = "0.2"
wasm-bindgen-futures = "0.4"
js-sys = "0.3"
web-sys = { version = "0.3", features = ["console"] }
getrandom = { version = "0.3", features = ["wasm_js"] }
<hick:when test="sqlite">sqlite-wasm-rs = { version = "0.4", default-features = false, features = ["precompiled"] }
uuid = { version = "1", features = ["v4", "serde", "js"] }
</hick:when>

# UniFFI for native FFI bindings (excluded from wasm32)
[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))'.dependencies]
uniffi = { version = "0.29", features = ["cli"] }
<hick:when test="sqlite">rusqlite = { version = "0.32", features = ["bundled"] }
uuid = { version = "1", features = ["v4", "serde"] }
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">iroh = "0.31"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["rt-multi-thread", "sync", "macros"] }
rand = "0.8"
url = "2"
</hick:when>

[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))'.build-dependencies]
uniffi = { version = "0.29", features = ["build"] }

[[bin]]
name = "uniffi-bindgen"
path = "src/bin/uniffi-bindgen.rs"

[features]
default = []
</hick:file>

### Rust Toolchain

We use nightly Rust for the latest features:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/rust-toolchain.toml">[toolchain]
channel = "nightly"
targets = ["wasm32-unknown-unknown"]
</hick:file>

### Build Script

The build script generates UniFFI bindings for native targets:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/build.rs">#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
fn main() {
    uniffi::generate_scaffolding("src/core.udl").unwrap();
}

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
fn main() {
    // No build script needed for WASM
}
</hick:file>

### UniFFI Interface Definition

The `.udl` file defines the FFI interface that UniFFI uses to generate bindings for
Swift, Kotlin, and C#:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/core.udl">namespace <hick:val name="project_name" />_core {
    string greet(string name);
    u64 fibonacci(u32 n);
    string process_data(string json_input);
<hick:when test="sqlite">
    // Database operations
    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    Database open_database(string path);
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">
    // Iroh networking operations
    [Throws=IrohError]
    IrohNode create_iroh_node(string? relay_url);

    string get_node_id([ByRef] IrohNode node);
</hick:when>
};

[Error]
enum CoreError {
    "InvalidInput",
    "ProcessingFailed",
};

dictionary GreetingResult {
    string message;
    u64 timestamp;
};
<hick:when test="sqlite">
[Error]
enum DatabaseError {
    "ConnectionFailed",
    "QueryFailed",
    "NotFound",
    "InvalidData",
};
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">
[Error]
enum IrohError {
    "InitFailed",
    "ConnectionFailed",
    "InvalidNodeId",
    "SendFailed",
    "ReceiveFailed",
};

dictionary NodeInfo {
    string node_id;
    string? relay_url;
    sequence<string> direct_addresses;
};

interface IrohNode {
    // Get this node's public identifier
    string node_id();

    // Get the relay URL this node is connected to
    string? relay_url();

    // Get node addressing info for sharing with peers
    [Throws=IrohError]
    NodeInfo node_info();

    // Connect to a peer by their node ID
    [Throws=IrohError]
    void connect(string node_id, string? relay_url);

    // Send data to a connected peer
    [Throws=IrohError]
    void send(string node_id, string alpn, bytes data);

    // Shutdown the node
    void shutdown();
};
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="sqlite">
dictionary TodoItem {
    string id;
    string title;
    boolean completed;
    string created_at;
};

interface Database {
    // Todo CRUD operations - returns JSON for cross-platform compatibility
    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    string create_todo(string title);

    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    string list_todos();

    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    string? get_todo(string id);

    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    string update_todo(string id, string? title, boolean? completed);

    [Throws=DatabaseError]
    void delete_todo(string id);

    // Close database connection
    void close();
};
</hick:when>
</hick:file>

### Core Library Implementation

The main library file contains the shared business logic. Functions are exposed to both
WASM (via wasm-bindgen) and native platforms (via UniFFI):

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/lib.rs">//! <hick:val name="project_name" /> Core Library
//!
//! Shared business logic that compiles to WebAssembly and native FFI bindings.

mod error;
<hick:when test="sqlite">mod database;
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
mod networking;
</hick:when>
pub use error::CoreError;
<hick:when test="sqlite">pub use database::{Database, DatabaseError, TodoItem, open_database};
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh">#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
pub use networking::{IrohNode, IrohError, NodeInfo, create_iroh_node, get_node_id};
</hick:when>

use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

// Include UniFFI scaffolding for native targets
#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
uniffi::include_scaffolding!("core");

// WASM bindings
#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
use wasm_bindgen::prelude::*;

/// Result type for greeting operations
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct GreetingResult {
    pub message: String,
    pub timestamp: u64,
}

/// Generate a personalized greeting
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `name` - The name to greet
///
/// # Returns
/// A greeting string
#[cfg_attr(target_arch = "wasm32", wasm_bindgen)]
pub fn greet(name: String) -> String {
    if name.is_empty() {
        "Hello, World!".to_string()
    } else {
        format!("Hello, {}!", name)
    }
}

/// Calculate the nth Fibonacci number
///
/// Uses an iterative approach for efficiency.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `n` - The index of the Fibonacci number to calculate
///
/// # Returns
/// The nth Fibonacci number
#[cfg_attr(target_arch = "wasm32", wasm_bindgen)]
pub fn fibonacci(n: u32) -> u64 {
    match n {
        0 => 0,
        1 => 1,
        _ => {
            let mut a = 0u64;
            let mut b = 1u64;
            for _ in 2..=n {
                let temp = a + b;
                a = b;
                b = temp;
            }
            b
        }
    }
}

/// Process JSON input and return transformed JSON output
///
/// This demonstrates more complex data handling across the FFI boundary.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `json_input` - A JSON string containing input data
///
/// # Returns
/// A JSON string with processed results
#[cfg_attr(target_arch = "wasm32", wasm_bindgen)]
pub fn process_data(json_input: String) -> String {
    let json_input = json_input.as_str();
    #[derive(Deserialize)]
    struct Input {
        values: Vec<i32>,
    }

    #[derive(Serialize)]
    struct Output {
        sum: i64,
        count: usize,
        average: f64,
        sorted: Vec<i32>,
    }

    let result: Result<Output, serde_json::Error> = (|| {
        let input: Input = serde_json::from_str(json_input)?;
        let sum: i64 = input.values.iter().map(|&x| x as i64).sum();
        let count = input.values.len();
        let average = if count > 0 {
            sum as f64 / count as f64
        } else {
            0.0
        };
        let mut sorted = input.values.clone();
        sorted.sort();

        Ok(Output {
            sum,
            count,
            average,
            sorted,
        })
    })();

    match result {
        Ok(output) => serde_json::to_string(&output).unwrap_or_else(|_| "{}".to_string()),
        Err(_) => r#"{"error": "Failed to process input"}"#.to_string(),
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_greet_with_name() {
        assert_eq!(greet("Alice".to_string()), "Hello, Alice!");
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_greet_empty_name() {
        assert_eq!(greet(String::new()), "Hello, World!");
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_fibonacci() {
        assert_eq!(fibonacci(0), 0);
        assert_eq!(fibonacci(1), 1);
        assert_eq!(fibonacci(10), 55);
        assert_eq!(fibonacci(20), 6765);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_process_data() {
        let input = r#"{"values": [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]}"#.to_string();
        let output = process_data(input);
        let parsed: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(&output).unwrap();

        assert_eq!(parsed["sum"], 31);
        assert_eq!(parsed["count"], 8);
        assert_eq!(parsed["sorted"], serde_json::json!([1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9]));
    }
}
</hick:file>

### Error Types

Error handling that works across FFI boundaries:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/error.rs">//! Error types for the core library

use thiserror::Error;

/// Errors that can occur in core library operations
#[derive(Error, Debug)]
pub enum CoreError {
    #[error("Invalid input: {0}")]
    InvalidInput(String),

    #[error("Processing failed: {0}")]
    ProcessingFailed(String),
}
</hick:file>

<hick:when test="sqlite">
### Database Module

The database module provides SQLite-backed storage for all platforms:
- Native: Uses rusqlite with bundled SQLite
- WASM: Uses sqlite-wasm-rs with precompiled SQLite for WebAssembly

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/database.rs">//! Database module with SQLite support for all platforms
//!
//! - Native: Uses rusqlite with bundled SQLite
//! - WASM: Uses sqlite-wasm-rs with precompiled SQLite

use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use thiserror::Error;
use uuid::Uuid;
use chrono::Utc;
use std::sync::Arc;

#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
use rusqlite::{Connection, params};
#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
use std::sync::Mutex;

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
use sqlite_wasm_rs as ffi;
#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
use std::ffi::CString;
#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
use std::cell::RefCell;

/// Database errors
#[derive(Error, Debug)]
pub enum DatabaseError {
    #[error("Connection failed: {0}")]
    ConnectionFailed(String),

    #[error("Query failed: {0}")]
    QueryFailed(String),

    #[error("Not found")]
    NotFound,

    #[error("Invalid data: {0}")]
    InvalidData(String),
}

/// A todo item stored in the database
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct TodoItem {
    pub id: String,
    pub title: String,
    pub completed: bool,
    pub created_at: String,
}

// ============================================================================
// Native Implementation (SQLite)
// ============================================================================

#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
pub struct Database {
    conn: Arc<Mutex<Connection>>,
}

#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
impl Database {
    fn new(conn: Connection) -> Self {
        Self {
            conn: Arc::new(Mutex::new(conn)),
        }
    }

    /// Create a new todo item (returns JSON string)
    pub fn create_todo(&self, title: String) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        let id = Uuid::new_v4().to_string();
        let created_at = Utc::now().to_rfc3339();

        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        conn.execute(
            "INSERT INTO todos (id, title, completed, created_at) VALUES (?1, ?2, ?3, ?4)",
            params![id, title, false, created_at],
        ).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let item = TodoItem {
            id,
            title,
            completed: false,
            created_at,
        };
        serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    /// List all todos (returns JSON array string)
    pub fn list_todos(&self) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        let mut stmt = conn
            .prepare("SELECT id, title, completed, created_at FROM todos ORDER BY created_at DESC")
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let rows = stmt
            .query_map([], |row| {
                Ok(TodoItem {
                    id: row.get(0)?,
                    title: row.get(1)?,
                    completed: row.get(2)?,
                    created_at: row.get(3)?,
                })
            })
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let mut todos = Vec::new();
        for row in rows {
            todos.push(row.map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?);
        }
        serde_json::to_string(&todos).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    /// Get a specific todo by ID (returns JSON string or None)
    pub fn get_todo(&self, id: String) -> Result<Option<String>, DatabaseError> {
        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        let mut stmt = conn
            .prepare("SELECT id, title, completed, created_at FROM todos WHERE id = ?1")
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let mut rows = stmt
            .query_map(params![id], |row| {
                Ok(TodoItem {
                    id: row.get(0)?,
                    title: row.get(1)?,
                    completed: row.get(2)?,
                    created_at: row.get(3)?,
                })
            })
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        match rows.next() {
            Some(row) => {
                let item = row.map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
                let json = serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;
                Ok(Some(json))
            },
            None => Ok(None),
        }
    }

    /// Internal: Get a specific todo by ID as struct (for update operations)
    fn get_todo_internal(&self, id: String) -> Result<Option<TodoItem>, DatabaseError> {
        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        let mut stmt = conn
            .prepare("SELECT id, title, completed, created_at FROM todos WHERE id = ?1")
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let mut rows = stmt
            .query_map(params![id], |row| {
                Ok(TodoItem {
                    id: row.get(0)?,
                    title: row.get(1)?,
                    completed: row.get(2)?,
                    created_at: row.get(3)?,
                })
            })
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        match rows.next() {
            Some(row) => Ok(Some(row.map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?)),
            None => Ok(None),
        }
    }

    /// Update a todo item (returns JSON string)
    pub fn update_todo(
        &self,
        id: String,
        title: Option<String>,
        completed: Option<bool>,
    ) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        let existing = self.get_todo_internal(id.clone())?.ok_or(DatabaseError::NotFound)?;

        let new_title = title.unwrap_or(existing.title);
        let new_completed = completed.unwrap_or(existing.completed);

        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        conn.execute(
            "UPDATE todos SET title = ?1, completed = ?2 WHERE id = ?3",
            params![new_title, new_completed, id],
        ).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let item = TodoItem {
            id,
            title: new_title,
            completed: new_completed,
            created_at: existing.created_at,
        };
        serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    /// Delete a todo item
    pub fn delete_todo(&self, id: String) -> Result<(), DatabaseError> {
        let conn = self.conn.lock().map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;
        let rows = conn
            .execute("DELETE FROM todos WHERE id = ?1", params![id])
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        if rows == 0 {
            return Err(DatabaseError::NotFound);
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Close the database connection
    pub fn close(&self) {
        // Connection is closed when dropped
    }
}

/// Open a database connection
#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
pub fn open_database(path: String) -> Result<Arc<Database>, DatabaseError> {
    let conn = Connection::open(&path)
        .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::ConnectionFailed(e.to_string()))?;

    // Create tables if they don't exist
    conn.execute(
        "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS todos (
            id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
            title TEXT NOT NULL,
            completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
            created_at TEXT NOT NULL
        )",
        [],
    ).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::QueryFailed(e.to_string()))?;

    Ok(Arc::new(Database::new(conn)))
}

// ============================================================================
// WASM Implementation (sqlite-wasm-rs)
// ============================================================================

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
pub struct Database {
    db: RefCell<*mut ffi::sqlite3>,
}

// Safety: Database is only used single-threaded in WASM
#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
unsafe impl Send for Database {}
#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
unsafe impl Sync for Database {}

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
impl Database {
    fn new(db: *mut ffi::sqlite3) -> Self {
        Self { db: RefCell::new(db) }
    }

    fn exec(&self, sql: &str) -> Result<(), DatabaseError> {
        let c_sql = CString::new(sql).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;
        let db = *self.db.borrow();
        let ret = unsafe {
            ffi::sqlite3_exec(db, c_sql.as_ptr(), None, std::ptr::null_mut(), std::ptr::null_mut())
        };
        if ret != ffi::SQLITE_OK {
            return Err(DatabaseError::QueryFailed(format!("sqlite error: {}", ret)));
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    pub fn create_todo(&self, title: String) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        let id = Uuid::new_v4().to_string();
        let created_at = Utc::now().to_rfc3339();

        let sql = format!(
            "INSERT INTO todos (id, title, completed, created_at) VALUES ('{}', '{}', 0, '{}')",
            id.replace("'", "''"),
            title.replace("'", "''"),
            created_at.replace("'", "''")
        );
        self.exec(&sql)?;

        let item = TodoItem {
            id,
            title,
            completed: false,
            created_at,
        };
        serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn list_todos(&self) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        let db = *self.db.borrow();
        let sql = CString::new("SELECT id, title, completed, created_at FROM todos ORDER BY created_at DESC")
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;

        let mut stmt: *mut ffi::sqlite3_stmt = std::ptr::null_mut();
        let ret = unsafe {
            ffi::sqlite3_prepare_v2(db, sql.as_ptr(), -1, &mut stmt, std::ptr::null_mut())
        };
        if ret != ffi::SQLITE_OK {
            return Err(DatabaseError::QueryFailed(format!("prepare error: {}", ret)));
        }

        let mut todos = Vec::new();
        loop {
            let step = unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_step(stmt) };
            if step == ffi::SQLITE_DONE {
                break;
            }
            if step != ffi::SQLITE_ROW {
                unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_finalize(stmt); }
                return Err(DatabaseError::QueryFailed(format!("step error: {}", step)));
            }

            let id = unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 0);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            };
            let title = unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 1);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            };
            let completed = unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_column_int(stmt, 2) != 0 };
            let created_at = unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 3);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            };

            todos.push(TodoItem { id, title, completed, created_at });
        }
        unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_finalize(stmt); }

        serde_json::to_string(&todos).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn get_todo(&self, id: String) -> Result<Option<String>, DatabaseError> {
        let db = *self.db.borrow();
        let sql = CString::new("SELECT id, title, completed, created_at FROM todos WHERE id = ?")
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;

        let mut stmt: *mut ffi::sqlite3_stmt = std::ptr::null_mut();
        let ret = unsafe {
            ffi::sqlite3_prepare_v2(db, sql.as_ptr(), -1, &mut stmt, std::ptr::null_mut())
        };
        if ret != ffi::SQLITE_OK {
            return Err(DatabaseError::QueryFailed(format!("prepare error: {}", ret)));
        }

        let c_id = CString::new(id).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;
        unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_bind_text(stmt, 1, c_id.as_ptr(), -1, ffi::SQLITE_TRANSIENT()); }

        let step = unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_step(stmt) };
        if step == ffi::SQLITE_DONE {
            unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_finalize(stmt); }
            return Ok(None);
        }
        if step != ffi::SQLITE_ROW {
            unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_finalize(stmt); }
            return Err(DatabaseError::QueryFailed(format!("step error: {}", step)));
        }

        let item = TodoItem {
            id: unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 0);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            },
            title: unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 1);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            },
            completed: unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_column_int(stmt, 2) != 0 },
            created_at: unsafe {
                let ptr = ffi::sqlite3_column_text(stmt, 3);
                if ptr.is_null() { String::new() } else {
                    std::ffi::CStr::from_ptr(ptr as *const i8).to_string_lossy().into_owned()
                }
            },
        };
        unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_finalize(stmt); }

        let json = serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;
        Ok(Some(json))
    }

    pub fn update_todo(
        &self,
        id: String,
        title: Option<String>,
        completed: Option<bool>,
    ) -> Result<String, DatabaseError> {
        // First get the existing todo
        let existing_json = self.get_todo(id.clone())?.ok_or(DatabaseError::NotFound)?;
        let existing: TodoItem = serde_json::from_str(&existing_json)
            .map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))?;

        let new_title = title.unwrap_or(existing.title);
        let new_completed = completed.unwrap_or(existing.completed);

        let sql = format!(
            "UPDATE todos SET title = '{}', completed = {} WHERE id = '{}'",
            new_title.replace("'", "''"),
            if new_completed { 1 } else { 0 },
            id.replace("'", "''")
        );
        self.exec(&sql)?;

        let item = TodoItem {
            id,
            title: new_title,
            completed: new_completed,
            created_at: existing.created_at,
        };
        serde_json::to_string(&item).map_err(|e| DatabaseError::InvalidData(e.to_string()))
    }

    pub fn delete_todo(&self, id: String) -> Result<(), DatabaseError> {
        let sql = format!("DELETE FROM todos WHERE id = '{}'", id.replace("'", "''"));
        self.exec(&sql)?;
        // Note: We don't check if the row existed, matching rusqlite behavior
        Ok(())
    }

    pub fn close(&self) {
        let db = *self.db.borrow();
        if !db.is_null() {
            unsafe { ffi::sqlite3_close(db); }
        }
    }
}

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
impl Drop for Database {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        self.close();
    }
}

#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
pub fn open_database(_path: String) -> Result<Arc<Database>, DatabaseError> {
    // WASM uses in-memory SQLite database
    let c_path = CString::new(":memory:").unwrap();
    let mut db: *mut ffi::sqlite3 = std::ptr::null_mut();

    let ret = unsafe {
        ffi::sqlite3_open_v2(
            c_path.as_ptr(),
            &mut db,
            ffi::SQLITE_OPEN_READWRITE | ffi::SQLITE_OPEN_CREATE,
            std::ptr::null()
        )
    };

    if ret != ffi::SQLITE_OK {
        return Err(DatabaseError::ConnectionFailed(format!("sqlite open error: {}", ret)));
    }

    let database = Database::new(db);

    // Create tables
    database.exec(
        "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS todos (
            id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
            title TEXT NOT NULL,
            completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
            created_at TEXT NOT NULL
        )"
    )?;

    Ok(Arc::new(database))
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_todo_crud() {
        let db = open_database(":memory:".to_string()).unwrap();

        // Create
        let todo_json = db.create_todo("Test task".to_string()).unwrap();
        let todo: TodoItem = serde_json::from_str(&todo_json).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(todo.title, "Test task");
        assert!(!todo.completed);

        // Read
        let todos_json = db.list_todos().unwrap();
        let todos: Vec<TodoItem> = serde_json::from_str(&todos_json).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(todos.len(), 1);

        // Update
        let updated_json = db.update_todo(todo.id.clone(), None, Some(true)).unwrap();
        let updated: TodoItem = serde_json::from_str(&updated_json).unwrap();
        assert!(updated.completed);

        // Delete
        db.delete_todo(todo.id).unwrap();
        let todos_json = db.list_todos().unwrap();
        let todos: Vec<TodoItem> = serde_json::from_str(&todos_json).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(todos.len(), 0);
    }
}
</hick:file>
</hick:when>

<hick:when test="iroh">
### Networking Module (Iroh)

The networking module provides peer-to-peer connectivity using Iroh. This is only
available on native platforms (not WASM) due to Iroh's networking requirements.

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/networking.rs">//! Iroh P2P networking module
//!
//! Provides peer-to-peer connectivity using Iroh for native platforms.
//! Iroh handles NAT traversal, hole punching, and relay fallback automatically.

use std::sync::Arc;
use thiserror::Error;
use iroh::{Endpoint, NodeAddr, NodeId, SecretKey};
use iroh_base::key::PublicKey;
use tokio::runtime::Runtime;
use std::str::FromStr;

/// Errors that can occur in Iroh networking operations
#[derive(Error, Debug)]
pub enum IrohError {
    #[error("Initialization failed: {0}")]
    InitFailed(String),

    #[error("Connection failed: {0}")]
    ConnectionFailed(String),

    #[error("Invalid node ID: {0}")]
    InvalidNodeId(String),

    #[error("Send failed: {0}")]
    SendFailed(String),

    #[error("Receive failed: {0}")]
    ReceiveFailed(String),
}

/// Information about a node for sharing with peers
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub struct NodeInfo {
    pub node_id: String,
    pub relay_url: Option<String>,
    pub direct_addresses: Vec<String>,
}

/// An Iroh networking node
pub struct IrohNode {
    endpoint: Endpoint,
    runtime: Arc<Runtime>,
    secret_key: SecretKey,
}

impl IrohNode {
    /// Get this node's public identifier (NodeId)
    pub fn node_id(&self) -> String {
        self.endpoint.node_id().to_string()
    }

    /// Get the relay URL this node is connected to
    pub fn relay_url(&self) -> Option<String> {
        self.runtime.block_on(async {
            self.endpoint.home_relay().map(|url| url.to_string())
        })
    }

    /// Get node addressing info for sharing with peers
    pub fn node_info(&self) -> Result<NodeInfo, IrohError> {
        self.runtime.block_on(async {
            let node_addr = self.endpoint.node_addr().await
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::InitFailed(e.to_string()))?;

            Ok(NodeInfo {
                node_id: node_addr.node_id.to_string(),
                relay_url: node_addr.relay_url.map(|u| u.to_string()),
                direct_addresses: node_addr.direct_addresses
                    .iter()
                    .map(|a| a.to_string())
                    .collect(),
            })
        })
    }

    /// Connect to a peer by their node ID
    pub fn connect(&self, node_id: String, relay_url: Option<String>) -> Result<(), IrohError> {
        let node_id = NodeId::from_str(&node_id)
            .map_err(|e| IrohError::InvalidNodeId(e.to_string()))?;

        let relay_url = relay_url
            .map(|url| url.parse())
            .transpose()
            .map_err(|e: url::ParseError| IrohError::ConnectionFailed(e.to_string()))?;

        let node_addr = NodeAddr {
            node_id,
            relay_url,
            direct_addresses: Default::default(),
        };

        self.runtime.block_on(async {
            // Use a default ALPN for the connection
            let alpn = b"<hick:val name="project_name" />/1";
            self.endpoint.connect(node_addr, alpn)
                .await
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::ConnectionFailed(e.to_string()))?;
            Ok(())
        })
    }

    /// Send data to a connected peer
    pub fn send(&self, node_id: String, alpn: String, data: Vec<u8>) -> Result<(), IrohError> {
        let node_id = NodeId::from_str(&node_id)
            .map_err(|e| IrohError::InvalidNodeId(e.to_string()))?;

        let node_addr = NodeAddr {
            node_id,
            relay_url: None,
            direct_addresses: Default::default(),
        };

        self.runtime.block_on(async {
            let conn = self.endpoint.connect(node_addr, alpn.as_bytes())
                .await
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::ConnectionFailed(e.to_string()))?;

            let mut send_stream = conn.open_uni()
                .await
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::SendFailed(e.to_string()))?;

            send_stream.write_all(&data)
                .await
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::SendFailed(e.to_string()))?;

            send_stream.finish()
                .map_err(|e| IrohError::SendFailed(e.to_string()))?;

            Ok(())
        })
    }

    /// Shutdown the node
    pub fn shutdown(&self) {
        self.runtime.block_on(async {
            self.endpoint.close().await;
        });
    }
}

/// Create a new Iroh node
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `relay_url` - Optional custom relay server URL. If None, uses Iroh's default relays.
pub fn create_iroh_node(relay_url: Option<String>) -> Result<Arc<IrohNode>, IrohError> {
    let runtime = Runtime::new()
        .map_err(|e| IrohError::InitFailed(e.to_string()))?;

    let secret_key = SecretKey::generate(rand::rngs::OsRng);

    let endpoint = runtime.block_on(async {
        let mut builder = Endpoint::builder()
            .secret_key(secret_key.clone());

        // If a custom relay URL is provided, configure it
        if let Some(url) = relay_url {
            let relay_url: iroh::RelayUrl = url.parse()
                .map_err(|e: url::ParseError| IrohError::InitFailed(e.to_string()))?;
            builder = builder.relay_mode(iroh::RelayMode::Custom(
                iroh::RelayMap::from_iter([iroh::RelayNode {
                    url: relay_url,
                    quic: None,
                }])
            ));
        }

        builder.bind()
            .await
            .map_err(|e| IrohError::InitFailed(e.to_string()))
    })?;

    Ok(Arc::new(IrohNode {
        endpoint,
        runtime: Arc::new(runtime),
        secret_key,
    }))
}

/// Get the node ID from an IrohNode (convenience function for FFI)
pub fn get_node_id(node: &IrohNode) -> String {
    node.node_id()
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_create_node() {
        let node = create_iroh_node(None).expect("should create node");
        let node_id = node.node_id();
        assert!(!node_id.is_empty());
        node.shutdown();
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_node_info() {
        let node = create_iroh_node(None).expect("should create node");
        let info = node.node_info().expect("should get node info");
        assert!(!info.node_id.is_empty());
        node.shutdown();
    }
}
</hick:file>
</hick:when>

### WASM-Specific TypeScript Bindings

For web platforms, we provide TypeScript type definitions. These are generated by
wasm-bindgen but we include a manual declaration file for better IDE support:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/pkg/types.d.ts">// TypeScript declarations for <hick:val name="project_name" />-core WASM module
// These augment the auto-generated wasm-bindgen types

declare module '<hick:val name="project_name" />-core' {
  /**
   * Initialize the WASM module
   * Must be called before using any other functions
   */
  export default function init(): Promise<void>;

  /**
   * Generate a personalized greeting
   * @param name - The name to greet (empty string returns default greeting)
   * @returns A greeting string
   */
  export function greet(name: string): string;

  /**
   * Calculate the nth Fibonacci number
   * @param n - The index (0-based) of the Fibonacci number
   * @returns The nth Fibonacci number as a bigint
   */
  export function fibonacci(n: number): bigint;

  /**
   * Process JSON data and return computed statistics
   * @param jsonInput - JSON string with { values: number[] }
   * @returns JSON string with { sum, count, average, sorted }
   */
  export function process_data(jsonInput: string): string;
<hick:when test="sqlite">
  /**
   * Open a database connection
   * @param path - Database path (ignored on WASM, uses in-memory)
   * @returns A Database instance
   */
  export function open_database(path: string): Database;

  /**
   * A todo item
   */
  export interface TodoItem {
    id: string;
    title: string;
    completed: boolean;
    created_at: string;
  }

  /**
   * Database interface for CRUD operations
   * Note: Methods return JSON strings that need to be parsed
   */
  export interface Database {
    /** Creates a todo and returns JSON string of TodoItem */
    create_todo(title: string): string;
    /** Returns JSON string of TodoItem[] */
    list_todos(): string;
    /** Returns JSON string of TodoItem or null */
    get_todo(id: string): string | null;
    /** Updates a todo and returns JSON string of TodoItem */
    update_todo(id: string, title: string | null, completed: boolean | null): string;
    delete_todo(id: string): void;
    close(): void;
  }
</hick:when>
}
</hick:file>

### Build Scripts

Scripts to build the core library for different targets:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/build-wasm.sh">#!/bin/bash
# Build WASM package for web platforms
# Requires: wasm-pack (cargo install wasm-pack)

set -e

echo "Building <hick:val name="project_name" />-core for WebAssembly..."

# Build with wasm-pack for bundler target (works with Vite)
wasm-pack build --target bundler --out-dir pkg

# Also build for web target (can be loaded directly in browser)
wasm-pack build --target web --out-dir pkg-web

echo "WASM build complete!"
echo "  - Bundler output: pkg/"
echo "  - Web output: pkg-web/"
</hick:file>

<hick:file path="rust-lib/build-native.sh">#!/bin/bash
# Build native libraries and generate FFI bindings
# Requires: uniffi-bindgen (cargo install uniffi_bindgen)

set -e

echo "Building <hick:val name="project_name" />-core for native platforms..."

# Build the native library
cargo build --release

# Generate Swift bindings
echo "Generating Swift bindings..."
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.dylib --language swift --out-dir bindings/swift 2>/dev/null || \
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.so --language swift --out-dir bindings/swift 2>/dev/null || \
echo "Swift binding generation requires macOS or Linux"

# Generate Kotlin bindings
echo "Generating Kotlin bindings..."
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.dylib --language kotlin --out-dir bindings/kotlin 2>/dev/null || \
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.so --language kotlin --out-dir bindings/kotlin 2>/dev/null || \
echo "Kotlin binding generation requires macOS or Linux"

# Generate C# bindings
echo "Generating C# bindings..."
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.dylib --language csharp --out-dir bindings/csharp 2>/dev/null || \
cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen generate --library target/release/lib<hick:val name="project_name" />_core.so --language csharp --out-dir bindings/csharp 2>/dev/null || \
echo "C# binding generation requires macOS or Linux"

echo "Native build complete!"
echo "Bindings generated in: bindings/"
</hick:file>

### UniFFI Bindgen Binary

A helper binary for generating bindings:

<hick:file path="rust-lib/src/bin/uniffi-bindgen.rs">//! UniFFI binding generator binary
//!
//! Run with: cargo run --bin uniffi-bindgen -- generate ...

fn main() {
    #[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]
    uniffi::uniffi_bindgen_main();

    #[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]
    panic!("uniffi-bindgen cannot run on wasm32 target");
}
</hick:file>

